, and sail area. The result is a fixed number, which is then referred to as the ship class. The class identifier for the 6 m class was an underlined “6”."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Three 6 metre boats competed in six races at the 1932 Olympics, so all teams won a medal. There was not much drama in this event, as the standings were the same in all six races. The Swedish yacht “Bissbi”, skippered by " [:a {:href "/athletes/62362"} "Tore Holm"] ", dominated the regatta, winning all the races and the gold medal. Equally clear was the silver medal for the United States boat, “Gallant”, which took second place in all races, while Canada’s “Caprice” was third throughout."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Race #1"] [:th {} "Race #2"] [:th {} "Race #3"] [:th {} "Race #4"] [:th {} "Race #5"] [:th {} "Race #6"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Bissbi"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "18"] [:td {} "3 (1)"] [:td {} "3 (1)"] [:td {} "3 (1)"] [:td {} "3 (1)"] [:td {} "3 (1)"] [:td {} "3 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "15"} [:a {:href "/athletes/62345"} "Martin Hindorff"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/61113"} "Olle Åkerlund"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/62362"} "Tore Holm"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/61319"} "Åke Bergqvist"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Gallant"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "12"] [:td {} "2 (2)"] [:td {} "2 (2)"] [:td {} "2 (2)"] [:td {} "2 (2)"] [:td {} "2 (2)"] [:td {} "2 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:cla